                '$`\\Delta \\mathrm{CE}_{k,\\mathrm{Wedge\\,1}} = \\mathrm{CE}_k\\left(\\Delta G_{\\mathrm{ECE},1}, \\Delta G_{\\mathrm{ECE},2}\\right) - \\Delta \\mathrm{CE}_{k,\\mathrm{ECE1}}^{\\mathrm{iso}} - \\Delta \\mathrm{CE}_{k,\\mathrm{Tuakana}}^{\\mathrm{iso}} = +3.19\\text{ pp CE}`$\n\n', ...
                '* **2. Tier 2 — Spatial, LVR & Enterprise Stack (+5.49%% CE Nat.) & Wedge 2 (`L07_WEDGE2_LVR_Whanau_Synergy` = +2.22%% CE Nat., 8.90%% Share):**\n', ...
                '   * *Isolated Factors:* Layer 4 ($`\\tau_a = 0.015`$ and $`\\tau_b: 0.25 \\to 0.18`$, yielding **+2.24%% CE**), Layer 5 (universal Age-20 Youth Capital Grant $`E: 0.065 \\to 0.080`$, yielding **+0.89%% CE**), and Layer 6 (Labrousse–Perdereau spatial transfer *T_k* + recycled carbon rebate, yielding **+0.15%% CE in *SS2* after 82%%–85%% transfer retirement** via $`T_k^{\\mathrm{SS2}} = T_k^{\\mathrm{SS0}} + (1 - \\psi_{\\mathrm{retire},T})(T_k^{\\mathrm{SS1}} - T_k^{\\mathrm{SS0}})`$ with $`\\psi_{\\mathrm{retire},T} = 0.850`$, recycling `-0.64 pp` of PAYE relief into Layer 10 [Ref 49, 56]).\n', ...
                '   * *Structural Complementarity Mechanism:* Young households transition from rental user cost $`r_{h,k}^{\\mathrm{rent}}`$ to homeowner user cost $`r_{h,k}^{\\mathrm{own}} = r_{h,k}^{\\mathrm{rent}} - \\psi_{\\mathrm{own}} Q_k`$ if and only if initial net worth clears the non-linear Kiyotaki et al. (2024) 20%% LVR down-payment threshold ($`a_1 + E \\ge \\xi_k Q_k(\\tau_a, \\tau_b)`$, $`\\xi_k = 0.20`$):\n\n', ...
                '$`\\Delta \\mathrm{CE}_{k,\\mathrm{Wedge\\,2}} = \\mathrm{CE}_k\\left(\\mathbf{\\Phi}_{\\mathrm{Spatial}}\\right) - \\left(\\Delta \\mathrm{CE}_{k,\\mathrm{TaxRebal}}^{\\mathrm{iso}} + \\Delta \\mathrm{CE}_{k,E}^{\\mathrm{iso}} + \\Delta \\mathrm{CE}_{k,T}^{\\mathrm{iso}}\\right) = +2.22\\text{ pp CE}`$\n\n', ...
                '* **3. Tier 3 — Cross-Stack Human Capital × Spatial/Enterprise Interaction (`L08_WEDGE3_CrossStack_HC_x_Spatial` = +4.79%% CE Nat., +5.36%% Akl, 19.22%% Share):**\n', ...
                '   * *Structural Complementarity Mechanism:* Captures four general-equilibrium cross-derivatives between $`\\mathbf{\\Phi}_{\\mathrm{HC}}`$ and $`\\mathbf{\\Phi}_{\\mathrm{Spatial}}`$: (i) *Firm–Worker Assortative Matching* ($`\\frac{\\partial^2 Y_k}{\\partial Z_k \\partial H_k} > 0`$); (ii) *Domestic Graduate Retention* in the $`4 \\times 5`$ Gumbel sorting operator $`\\Pi_{\\mathrm{mig}}`$ ($`\\sim 3,550`$ skilled graduates/yr retained); (iii) *Relief of the Kaiako Housing-Affordability Supply Deflator* $`G_{\\mathrm{ECE}}^{\\mathrm{eff}}(Q_k)`$; and (iv) **Regional $`z_\\ell \\to z_h`$ Job Upgrading & Monopsony Relief** ($`\\Delta \\mu_{z,k} > 0`$, [Ref 29, 49, 56]), where breaking farm-gate wholesale monopsony and anchoring `1.60x–2.16x` local food-hub procurement multipliers shifts rural and provincial workers from low-wage $`z_\\ell`$ draws into high-productivity $`z_h`$ enterprises, allowing 82%%–85%% of the *SS1* geographic transfer to retire:\n\n', ...
